@startuml UC-SEMANTIC-KEY
' UC-00 - Use Case Name | semantic key: UC-SEMANTIC-KEY
' Source: data/use_cases/<domain>/UC-SEMANTIC-KEY.yml
' Business Rules: BR-...
' Trace comments ' [ref] name the YAML element behind the next action.
' No title: the Word caption supplies it.
' Illustrative NF/AF/EX blocks below are OPTIONAL. Replace or remove every example
' after mapping this UC's YAML and Business Rules; never copy UC-24.2 logic.
!include ../../_shared/activity-style.puml

' Declare every partition once, with an alias, before start.
' Replace Developer with this UC's primary actor; add an external-service lane only if used.
|DEV| $lane_title("Developer")
|SYS| $lane_title("System")

|DEV|
start
' [NF1]
:Verb the object;
|SYS|
' [NF2]
:Validate the request;
' OPTIONAL AF retry example: remove unless this UC has a correction/resubmission flow.
' Both guards are labelled; every resubmission is validated before the next test.
while ($question("Information invalid?")) is ($guard_left("[invalid — AF-01]"))
  ' [AF-01.1]
  :Identify the invalid information;
  |DEV|
  ' [AF-01.2]
  :Correct the information;
  |SYS|
  ' [NF2, AF-01] Re-perform the UC's validation step after resubmission.
  :Validate the corrected information;
endwhile ($guard("[valid]"))
' OPTIONAL EX example: remove unless this UC has the matching exception.
' Exception is not a silent end; the last action states its outcome.
if ($question("Item still available?")) then ($guard_left("[available]"))
else ($guard_right("[no longer", "available — EX-01]"))
  ' [EX-01, GUIDE-7.3] Use GUIDE-7.3 only when the spec omits the outcome.
  :Report the request was not completed;
  stop
endif
' [NF3, POST1]
:Store the result;
' [POST2]
:Record the change in
activity history;
stop
@enduml
